mmdevapi: spatial audio on a device with fewer channels than the bed.

GTA V Enhanced stopped at launch with "Failed to initialize spatial audio
client. Please ensure that your audio device is setup correctly." The
session log shows the device the stream was opened against:

    aaudio: shared, burst 868, capacity 1736, 48000 Hz x2, format 1

ActivateSpatialAudioStream opens one IAudioClient with a channel per static
object the caller asked for (a 7.1.4 bed is 12), in shared mode. wineoss
(0008) refuses more than 8 channels outright and fails any count AAudio
does not grant exactly, and the phone's output is stereo, so Initialize
fails and the game reports the error. GE-Proton fixed the same thing in
winealsa (WINEALSA_SPATIAL); there is no winealsa here.

Three changes, none specific to wineoss:

1. When Initialize with the requested layout fails, the stream reopens in
   the device's own mix-format layout and downmixes into it: a speaker the
   device has is copied straight through, a missing one is folded onto the
   front left/right at -3 dB (centre onto both), LFE is dropped. With a
   device that takes the full bed, nothing changes.
2. IsSpatialAudioStreamAvailable answered E_NOTIMPL and
   GetNativeStaticObjectTypeMask E_NOTIMPL. Both now report the object
   render stream and a 7.1.4 bed as available, which (1) makes true.
3. static_mask_to_channels gave BackCenter map slot 12 while
   AudioObjectType_to_index returns 16 for it, so a BackCenter object was
   never mixed. Routes are now indexed the same way objects are.

The render buffer is also cleared at the start of each update, since
objects are summed into it.

